# Hits: line 9 (if/else, both branches assign the same target) and line 17
# (X := IfThen(C, 1, 2) -- call form with two inert literal branches, so the
# if-expression is behaviour-identical).
# Non-hits: 18 (IfThen with a non-literal branch: IfThen evaluates both
# arguments, an if-expression only one, so the swap is not equivalent -- that
# shape belongs to ifthen-both-branches), 23 (already an if-expression, no
# statement if), 24 (branches assign different targets), 28 (no else),
# 30 (else branch is not an assignment).
# Known FP shape: compound targets (A.B := ..) fire when both sides match.
ifthen-to-if-expression 9
ifthen-to-if-expression 17
!ifthen-to-if-expression 18
!ifthen-to-if-expression 23
!ifthen-to-if-expression 24
!ifthen-to-if-expression 28
!ifthen-to-if-expression 30